{
  // Output filename and BoardLoader data-variable name:
  //   boardName "RP2350" -> designer/boards/RP2350/RP2350.json -> const RP2350Data = {...}
  "boardName": "RP2350",

  // Fallback human-readable name shown in the designer UI.  Overridden
  // by the matching `<id>.name=` entry in a sibling-or-ancestor
  // boards.txt when one is present (matched via `<id>.build.variant=`
  // against this variant's directory name).
  "displayName": "Raspberry Pi Pico 2 (RP2350)",

  // Same pin-declaration style as RP2040 — shares the "rp2040" family
  // value (see variants/rp2040/rp2040/board.json for the full rationale)
  // so this stays grouped under the same Designer family, split out as
  // its own "chip" bucket.
  "family": "rp2040",

  "inputOnlyGpios": [],

  // Default transports — Serial only. No WiFi on this chip variant.
  "connections": ["serial"],

  // RP2040/RP2350 boot from an internal ROM/BOOTSEL, not GPIO-driven
  // flash-mode strapping pins like ESP32/ESP8266 — no boot-time
  // restrictions to flag at the chip level.
  "pinNotes": {},

  // pfodWeb NOTE (RP2040/RP2350 family button/LED/NeoPixel audit,
  // 2026-07-13):
  //
  // Board: Adafruit "Feather RP2350 with HSTX" (products 6000 / 6130 —
  // 6130 ships with 8MB PSRAM pre-installed, 6000 does not; both share the
  // identical pinout/PCB and this board's pins_arduino.h) — an Adafruit
  // Feather with an onboard 22-pin HSTX connector driven by the RP2350's
  // native HSTX peripheral (a dedicated hardware transmit block, successor
  // to the RP2040's PIO-bit-banged PicoDVI approach used on the sibling
  // adafruit_feather_dvi board), an optional onboard SOIC PSRAM footprint,
  // the usual plain status LED, and an onboard single status NeoPixel.
  // Unlike the RP2040-family Adafruit Feather DVI/SCORPIO boards, this
  // board's Boot/Reset buttons are NOT wired to a spare general-purpose
  // GPIO — see GPIO7 reasoning below.
  //
  // Sources consulted:
  // 1. https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-feather-rp2350/pinouts
  //    (official Adafruit guide, fetched directly) — quotes: "This little
  //    red LED is connected to GPIO7. This little red LED is controllable
  //    in CircuitPython code using board.LED, and in Arduino as PIN_LED."
  //    -> status LED = GPIO7. "Above the silkscreen label for pin SCK is
  //    the status NeoPixel LED. It is connected to GPIO21." -> onboard
  //    NeoPixel = GPIO21. "The chip select line for the PSRAM is broken
  //    out and is labeled PCS on the board silk. It is attached to GPIO8.
  //    If you have PSRAM onboard, DO NOT use GPIO8 as a regular GPIO!" ->
  //    PSRAM CS = GPIO8, explicitly reserved by Adafruit's own warning
  //    even on the non-PSRAM-populated variant (the CS trace/footprint is
  //    present on both). HSTX connector differential pairs: "D0P/GPIO18"
  //    /"D0N/GPIO19", "D1P/GPIO16"/"D1N/GPIO17", "D2P/GPIO12"/"D2N/GPIO13",
  //    "CKP/GPIO14"/"CKN/GPIO15" — exact match to this board's own
  //    pins_arduino.h PIN_CKN/CKP/D0N/D0P/D1N/D1P/D2N/D2P defines. Also
  //    confirms STEMMA QT SDA=GPIO2/SCL=GPIO3 as the board's I2C1 bus —
  //    the same Wire0 pins already broken out on the Feather header, not a
  //    separate dedicated pair (shared-bus arrangement).
  //    Boot/Reset buttons: "The Boot button is the button on the right...
  //    The Reset button is on the left." — described purely by physical
  //    location/function, with NO GPIO number given anywhere on this page
  //    (unlike GPIO7/LED, GPIO21/NeoPixel, GPIO8/PSRAM, which are all given
  //    explicit GPIO numbers) — consistent with these being the RP2350's
  //    dedicated non-GPIO BOOTSEL (QSPI_CS-monitored by the on-chip boot
  //    ROM) and RUN/reset hardware lines, not general-purpose GPIOs wired
  //    to switches (contrast with the sibling adafruit_feather_dvi/
  //    adafruit_feather_scorpio boards, whose BOOT button genuinely is a
  //    spare GPIO7 pulled to GND, and whose pins_arduino.h files declare a
  //    PIN_BUTTON accordingly) — this board's own pins_arduino.h has NO
  //    PIN_BUTTON define at all, corroborating that reading.
  // 2. https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-feather-rp2350/overview
  //    (official Adafruit guide, via WebFetch) — quotes: "a special High
  //    Speed Transmit (HSTX) peripheral that drives 4 lanes of
  //    differential data transmission such as DVI output" and "8 more
  //    'consecutive' GPIO available on the HSTX connector" (GPIO12-19) —
  //    confirms these 8 GPIOs are dedicated/reserved for the onboard HSTX
  //    connector, not general-purpose broken-out pins. Also: "Pin #7 red
  //    LED for general purpose blinking", "RGB NeoPixel for full-color
  //    indication", "Both Reset button and Bootloader select button for
  //    quick restarts", "Optional spot for SOIC PSRAM chip with chip
  //    select line on GPIO 8", and "21 GPIO available on the Feather
  //    header pins, 8 more 'consecutive' GPIO available on the HSTX
  //    connector" (21 + 8 = 29 total GPIO, matching this board's
  //    pins_arduino.h D/A alias count once GPIO8/12-19 are excluded).
  // 3. https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-feather-rp2350/frequently-asked-questions
  //    (official Adafruit guide, via WebFetch) — checked specifically for
  //    any GPIO-level detail on the red LED's active-high/low polarity or
  //    the Boot/Reset buttons' wiring; contains neither (only describes
  //    the separate NeoPixel status-color meaning) — no contradiction of
  //    source #1/#2's readings.
  // 4. https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adafruit/circuitpython/main/ports/raspberrypi/boards/adafruit_feather_rp2350/pins.c
  //    (fetched directly) — independently corroborates every pin mapping
  //    in this board's pins_arduino.h: MP_QSTR_LED -> pin_GPIO7,
  //    MP_QSTR_NEOPIXEL -> pin_GPIO21, MP_QSTR_CKN -> pin_GPIO15,
  //    MP_QSTR_CKP -> pin_GPIO14, MP_QSTR_D0N -> pin_GPIO19, MP_QSTR_D0P ->
  //    pin_GPIO18, MP_QSTR_D1N -> pin_GPIO17, MP_QSTR_D1P -> pin_GPIO16,
  //    MP_QSTR_D2N -> pin_GPIO13, MP_QSTR_D2P -> pin_GPIO12, MP_QSTR_SDA ->
  //    pin_GPIO2, MP_QSTR_SCL -> pin_GPIO3, MP_QSTR_SCK -> pin_GPIO22,
  //    MP_QSTR_MOSI -> pin_GPIO23, MP_QSTR_MISO -> pin_GPIO20 — this is an
  //    exact match to this board's Arduino pins_arduino.h aliases (SPI0
  //    MISO=20/MOSI=23/SCK=22, Wire0 SDA=2/SCL=3) — strong independent
  //    confirmation from a wholly separate vendor firmware codebase.
  //    Notably, this file defines NO MP_QSTR_BUTTON or MP_QSTR_BOOT entry
  //    at all — further corroborating that the Boot/Reset buttons are not
  //    exposed as regular named GPIOs on this board (contrast with the
  //    sibling adafruit_feather_rp2040_dvi pins.c, which DOES define both
  //    MP_QSTR_BUTTON and MP_QSTR_BOOT -> pin_GPIO7).
  // 5. https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adafruit/circuitpython/main/ports/raspberrypi/boards/adafruit_feather_rp2350/mpconfigboard.h
  //    (fetched directly) — confirms `#define MICROPY_HW_NEOPIXEL
  //    (&pin_GPIO21)` (no polarity/inverted flags needed for a NeoPixel
  //    data line), `#define CIRCUITPY_PSRAM_CHIP_SELECT (&pin_GPIO8)`,
  //    `DEFAULT_SPI_BUS_SCK/MOSI/MISO` = GPIO22/23/20 with NO chip-select
  //    #define at all (independently corroborating that this board's
  //    vendor-default PIN_SPI0_SS=21 in pins_arduino.h was a spurious
  //    unused default, not a genuine onboard SPI CS use — see GPIO21
  //    reasoning below), and `DEFAULT_DVI_BUS_CLK_DN/DP` = GPIO15/14,
  //    `_RED_DN/DP` = GPIO19/18, `_GREEN_DN/DP` = GPIO17/16, `_BLUE_DN/DP`
  //    = GPIO13/12 — an exact match to this board's PIN_CKN/CKP/D0N/D0P/
  //    D1N/D1P/D2N/D2P pins_arduino.h defines, confirming the full 8-pin
  //    HSTX/DVI GPIO12-19 assignment from a second independent source.
  // 6. No official Zephyr RTOS board port exists yet for this specific
  //    board (searched; only a community/Playground guide on writing one
  //    from scratch was found, and the closely-related "Adafruit Metro
  //    RP2350" Zephyr doc does not cover this Feather board's LED wiring)
  //    - so GPIO7 LED polarity is not independently confirmable via
  //    Zephyr devicetree the way earlier RP2040-family boards in this
  //    audit were. Treated as active-high on precedent: every Adafruit
  //    RP2040/RP2350 Feather-family board audited so far in this repo
  //    with a plain GPIO+resistor-to-GND status LED (rpipico,
  //    adafruit_feather_scorpio, adafruit_feather_dvi) uses the standard
  //    active-high wiring, and no contrary evidence was found for this
  //    board in any source above.
  //
  // Full findings/sources trail:
  // boardsDetails/rp2040/rp2350/adafruit_feather_rp2350_hstx/notes.txt
  "chipGpios": {
    "7":  { "capabilities": ["digital_output", "pwm_output", "led_high"], "note": "PIN_LED — onboard status LED, active-high" },
    "8":  { "capabilities": [], "note": "RP2350_PSRAM_CS — dedicated chip-select for onboard PSRAM" },
    "12": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_D2P — HSTX connector TMDS/DVI data-channel-2 plus" },
    "13": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_D2N — HSTX connector TMDS/DVI data-channel-2 minus" },
    "14": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_CKP — HSTX connector TMDS/DVI clock+ differential line" },
    "15": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_CKN — HSTX connector TMDS/DVI clock- differential line" },
    "16": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_D1P — HSTX connector TMDS/DVI data-channel-1 plus" },
    "17": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_D1N — HSTX connector TMDS/DVI data-channel-1 minus" },
    "18": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_D0P — HSTX connector TMDS/DVI data-channel-0 plus" },
    "19": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_D0N — HSTX connector TMDS/DVI data-channel-0 minus" },
    "21": { "capabilities": ["digital_output", "led_neopixel"], "note": "PIN_NEOPIXEL — onboard single status NeoPixel (WS2812)" }
  },

  // Same 8-bit analogWrite() default as every other RP2040/RP2350 board.
  "pwm": { "min": 0, "max": 255, "method": "analogWrite" },

  // No hardware DAC on RP2040/RP2350.
  "dac": {},

  // RP2350's one 12-bit ADC (0-4095), ~3.3V reference — same as every
  // other RP2040/RP2350 board. This board's pins_arduino.h declares its
  // own bespoke A0-A3 = GPIO26-29 mapping, matching the chip-level
  // default; no reason found to override.
  "adc": { "bits": 12, "max": 4095, "defaultRefVolts": "3.3" }
}
